1. Git & GitHub Basics
What is Git?
Git is a distributed version control system used to track code changes.
What is GitHub?
GitHub is a cloud platform used to store and manage Git repositories.
Difference between Git and GitHub?
Git → Version control tool
GitHub → Cloud hosting platform for Git repositories
What is a repository?
A repository is a storage location where project files and code history are maintained.
What is a commit?
A commit is a saved snapshot of code changes.
What is clone?
Clone copies a remote repository to the local machine.
Command:
Bash
git clone <repo-url>
